# tools/treasurybot: one live XMR payout round and one live ZEC payout round, 2026-09-13
#
# Nodes: monerod 0.18.5.1 --regtest (nettype fakechain) with two monero-wallet-rpc (treasury on 28083, payer on
# 28084, --disable-rpc-login); zebrad 6.3.0 on regtest (started and stopped again by tools/regtest/zcash-up.sh and
# zcash-down.sh); the DERO simulator (daemon 127.0.0.1:20000) and its Founders Pass v2 c588e98e… (share 5000 bps).
# Each asset step ran under tools/withlock.sh (xmrreg, zecreg). The steps are TestLiveRegtestRound in
# tools/treasurybot/payout_live_test.go (TREASURYBOT_LIVE=setup|xmr|zec|cleanup); journals and Zcash keys were kept
# in a scratch directory outside the repository (<tmp>). Paths are scrubbed; no key, login or tx_metadata is shown.
#
# What the test drives is the bot's own code: planPayouts and startPayouts (the flags' checks, get_address_index,
# the nodes' chain), then assetPayer.round twice: the first closes the period (income, snapshot at a DERO height,
# split) and sends the payout; the second, after 10 blocks, closes it as paid. The result is then checked from the
# holder's side: the payer wallet's own record of the incoming XMR, and the mined ZEC transaction's output.
#
# DERO spent from simulator wallet 30016 (the only wallet used): Mint(1) = 100000 atomic units (1 DERO, to the pass's
# treasury), plus the gas of Mint, Register, SetXmr, SetZec, two clearing calls and Withdraw. Its balance went from
# 199879 to 97442. The pass is kept by 30016, unregistered: the cleanup cleared both payout addresses and withdrew
# position 0, so hst is 0 again, as it was before.
#
# The XMR fee is a real 2 XMR transfer from the payer wallet to the treasury's dedicated subaddress. The ZEC fee is a
# regtest coinbase mined to zecTreasury (no swap has paid a ZEC fee on this chain; zebrad has no wallet), 38146
# zatoshi at this height, spendable after 100 blocks. The ZEC fee of the payout, 10000 zatoshi, is on the bot's
# "payout 1 sent" line; the "fee 0" on the later "live:" line is a display bug of that run's test (it read the fee
# from a parsed transaction whose inputs carry no values) and was removed from the test afterwards.
#
# The run was made on the branch's code before it was rebased onto main c707ff4 (the ZEC swap fee); the rebase
# changed only netcfg's field plumbing for zecTreasury, not the payout code.

